## One-use choreography and full inventory

Method authority explicitly allows candidate A max1, reader B max1 and witness C max1, each consumed0 and separately counted for actual spawn attempts/returned status. These helpers are process-only actor launches, not extra candidate retries. One total900-second monotonic budget begins at the FIRST actor spawn; at most30 seconds per peer observation and remaining budget; <=250ms polls. No budget reset, generic sleep or process guessing. Source-only stage must not expose an executable helper admission.

Launch B and C once with connected pipes, collect their exact runtime READY, then launch A once and collect its READY. Before A exists the complete inventory is PID1 plus currently admitted B/C; after A exists the exact inventory is sorted `[1,A,B,C]`. All are distinct canonical safe positive PIDs in the same owned container namespace. No top/PID order selection. Every helper uses builtin `fs.readdirSync('/proc')`, selects only canonical positive decimal directory names, bounds to4096/1MiB, and returns complete sorted actual numeric inventory. During a peer read no other target process is spawned. Threads are not silently accepted as extra processes; any unexpected directory/process requires UNKNOWN and preserved raw observation.

After all three READYs, caller sends each helper one PEERS frame binding nonce, A/B/C PIDs and exact raw READY hashes plus fixed role. Helpers require own PID equals their assigned role, all IDs distinct, and fixed expected source/Node/runtime identities. The frame conveys targets, not authority to choose arbitrary files. B may read only A or C as fixed next step; C may read only B. Each script hardcodes its permitted sequence and derives only canonical `/proc/<declared peer>` paths. Wrong target/step/nonce/PID/digest/duplicate/extra bytes/early EOF refuses.

PRE_START round, in this exact order: C reads full B bracket; B reads full C bracket; B reads full A bracket; C reads full B bracket again; B reads full C bracket again. Each read is one bounded pure-builtin operation in its already admitted actor, not a new Docker exec. POST_RESULT repeats those five actions after A's RESULT and before its EXIT. The two readings of each helper must have stable CID/PID/PPID/startTicks/argv/env/exe/Node/script/nonce, covering the A acquisition between them. Each internal bracket itself retains stat-before and stat-after. B's PRE/POST A tuples must also match. Independent C observes B's actual kernel identity; B observes C's actual identity. Neither observes itself. This terminates the helper proof without an unaccounted observer.

Inventory must be complete and exactly four processes at every observation, and every claimed actor has current connected raw READY plus full observed peer tuple. Capture PID1 inventory/tuple correlation from actual birth without substituting it for any actor. Helper roles/bytes are version2 actual source authority, never synthetic six-distinct-PID values.

## Exact helper wire and observation identity

Helper READY is a NEW closed11 record: ordinary candidate READY's nine fields plus `actorRole` exactly READER_B or WITNESS_C and `helperProtocolVersion` integer2. Its distinct script/source hash and exact logical argv are bound to the permit. It is not parsed as candidate READY. The ordinary five-field runtimeFence recipe remains compact ordered UTF8 JSON without LF; helper role/version are separately bound in the helper authority/READY bytes.

PEERS closed7: kind `EXTERNAL_HELPER_PEERS_V2`, nonce, actorRole, helperProtocolVersion, peers, readyHashes, expectedInventory. `peers` closed3 keys A/B/C with strict safe integers; `readyHashes` closed3 keys with exact prefixed hashes of the retained raw READY frames; inventory is exact sorted `[1,A,B,C]`. A helper checks its own raw READY SHA and assigned PID, then retains this in its protocol state. No host-supplied encoded executable or path.

OBSERVE command closed5: kind `EXTERNAL_HELPER_OBSERVE_V2`, nonce, actorRole, step, targetRole. Exact step sequence is PRE_B1, PRE_C1, PRE_A, PRE_B2, PRE_C2, then POST_B1, POST_C1, POST_A, POST_B2, POST_C2 on the combined caller timeline. C accepts only its four B steps; B only its six C/A steps. Commands have one LF, strict duplicate-free compact UTF8 JSON, <=16KiB and no additional buffered frame. Host sends only after the prior expected response is validated and retained.

OBSERVATION closed10: kind `EXTERNAL_HELPER_OBSERVATION_V2`, nonce, actorRole, step, targetRole, observerPid, targetPid, peersFrameSha256, commandFrameSha256, rawProof. The exact consumed command/PEERS hashes and own READY role/PID/source are checked by caller. `rawProof` closed8: statBefore, cmdline, environ, exeLink, exeSha256, exeBytes, statAfter, inventory. Four raw files are closed3 `{bytes,sha256,base64}` with canonical Base64 and exact decoded digest/size; read bounds64KiB each and no silent truncation. exeLink is literal string, exe digest from direct magic `/proc/<peer>/exe`, size strict positive <=33MiB checked before bounded read/hash. Inventory is complete source-bound actual names/numeric list, not desired membership. Full OBSERVATION <=1MiB; raw stderr stays empty. No filtering/reconstructed proc bytes.

Parser independently reparses actual stat before/after: exact known50 postcomm fields/oneLF, strict PID equal target, PPID bounds, safe positive startTicks<=2^53-1, individually live states. Decode full NUL cmdline/env; require fixed kernel argv/script/nonce, unique exact env3 and QEMU literal link/hash9376. Official Node89af/source/hash/loaders are separately checked in each READY and peer kernel argv. Compare immutable identity fields across brackets; dynamic stat counters/state need not be byte-identical but complete raw records remain. External access through helpers is still hypothetical, not proven by these DTOs.

Once both rounds finish, send helper FINAL closed5 kind `EXTERNAL_HELPER_EXIT_V2`, nonce, actorRole, peersFrameSha256, transcriptSha256. Transcript digest commits exactly that helper's ordered raw READY/PEERS/commands/observations including LF and direction framing. Require EOF and no trailing bytes; each helper exits0/emptyerr only after its finite steps. No generic EXIT or early helper closure. Helpers remain alive until after A exit/wait is retained, so the final candidate proof never uses vanished helper identity. Final inventory should return to PID1 only; owned stop/final sameCID inspect follows. Any missing helper or unknown extra process is UNKNOWN, not cleanup success.

