## Orchestration source closure and stopping rules

Implement new caller disabled first. Full command/raw receipt and evidence rules from accepted mechanisms apply to every one of three Popen calls and partial stream operation: literal argv/env, actual PID/times, no PTY, source/permit rehash, exclusive output fsync, exact attempts/returned counts, bounded incremental IO and original raw bytes. Signals set a flag; no late new actor/command/frame after it. Preserve stdout/stderr partials and stdin bytes on timeout/spawn/second cleanup errors, unknown waits, command closure and actual return. Constructor/clock inputs retain011c typed finite/nonnegative/nondecreasing controls. Record actual failed operation, not claimed phase success. Host mocks must show interruption immediately before each spawn/frame/fsync/return/handler restoration and no further forward steps.

Any error poisons the one attempt, no recover-and-continue after a refused phase. Close pipes and perform only qualified cleanup of ownership-admitted exact CID; stop exit/stderr/timeout and final actual sameCID nonrunning are required, unresolved-running remains quarantined. Any PID reuse/reexec/death/extra inventory/source or peer-authority drift/bad frame/digest/unknown stderr/partial raw/unsafe stop => UNKNOWN. Preserve immutable original OUTCOME, actual full returned disposition and additive late corrections; entry reconciles full typed content, not status alone. Final Exit137 is observation, not inferred TERM-only cause. No old runner restart/reuse, automatic retry, forced generic kill or unowned directory/container deletion.

